we hope you're ready folks because today  we're discussing the most dangerous scp  of all time we know you've probably  heard this before but seriously this one  is the absolute top of the pyramid of  fear or the fear amid if you will this  scp makes 682 weep and terror for its  life it makes the old man  scp-106 consider turning his life around  and taking up a career in humanitarian  work it even makes the dreaded scarlet  king himself the lord of chaos the  ultimate despair quake in his spiky red  boots it's just that utterly terrifying  just kidding it's lego but we had you  going there for a second didn't we  though it may not actually be the  scariest anomaly of all time  scp-387 isn't your granddad's lego set  either unless your granddad goes by  agent hardy and works for the scp  foundation hardy is one of the hundreds  of thousands of foundation field agents  planted all over the globe in everything  from law enforcement to surveillance  ever watchful for the kinds of anomalies  the scp foundation makes it their  mission to secure contain and protect  but when he discovered  scp-387 he wasn't even technically on  duty he was taking a long train journey  home from his parents house while his  car was in the shop and as anyone who's  ever taken a long train journey knows  without proper stimulation boredom will  crop up in no time he'd been reading a  pretty interesting book on his e-reader  when tragedy first struck and it ran out  of battery hardy had forgotten to bring  his charging cable so he was potentially  looking at another three hours of  mind-numbing monotony that's when he  noticed the red plastic tub that had  been apparently abandoned in the seat  across from him he realized in that  moment that had been there the whole  time unsupervised given that he was a  foundation field agent and was as such  extremely curious he grabbed the tub and  took a look inside hoping to find  something that'll quell his growing  boredom lucky for him the box was full  of lego bricks everyone's favorite brand  of toy construction block the tub was  brimming with a vast collection of  pieces some of which like wheels and  prisms agent hardy had never seen before  despite spending his childhood  obsessively making lego constructions  but hardy wasn't one to criticize a gift  from the universe this tub of lego  pieces would be the perfect way to keep  himself entertained for the rest of his  long journey he spent the next hour or  so meticulously recreating site 19 in  lego form on the table in front of him  when the building was done he decided to  have some fun and populate the site with  a collection of lego men standing in for  scp foundation scientists containment  specialists and guards after finding a  torso with a lab coat in the box agent  hardy decided to make a tiny dr bright  to start with however as soon as he made  the tiny lego scientist and set it down  on his new site 19 playset he realized  that everything was not as innocently  typical as it seemed the little man  instantly began to walk immediately  picking up a tiny lego clipboard and  heading towards the euclid containment  wing agent hardy had discovered a brand  new anomaly on his day off while playing  with toys on a boring train ride  philosopher l p jacks was certainly  right when he said a master in the art  of living draws no sharp distinction  between his work and his play naturally  agent hardy immediately took the little  lego man apart along with his site 19  simulacrum and alerted his superiors at  the scp foundation his co-workers met  him at the next train stop platform not  long after the box of seemingly living  lego pieces redesignated  scp-387 was in the hands of foundation  researcher dr arch his first priority  was finding out what exactly they were  all dealing with here whether there was  more of it out there and whether it was  dangerous attempts to investigate the  origins of scp-387 were mostly fruitless  undercover foundation agents  investigated every lego-producing  location they could find but found no  evidence of anything similar to 387  being produced and of course as with  anything that seemed to be an anomalous  toy all possible links to dr  wondertainment were also explored but  again nothing came up this was probably  for the best if 387 was a dr  wondertainment product it probably would  have built itself into an actual sized  dinosaur and started eating people  already all further investigations into  387's origins were subsequently dropped  with background research turning out to  be a dead end dr arch decided to get  down to business doing the fun part  actual experimentation after gathering  all the proper permissions from his  superiors the testing commenced in  experiment 387-8  dr arch recruited a number of  lego-loving d-classes after all even  convicted robbers arsonists and  murderers loved lego and made them  construct a little lego community inside  a testing chamber this consisted of a  small main street with a number of lego  stores a residential area and a bar as  soon as the d-classes constructed a  variety of little lego men and released  them into the community they instantly  came to life and began performing their  roles perfectly some took up jobs in the  various stores cafes and boutiques  others acted as patrons for the  different businesses the lego men were  even noted as forming rudimentary family  units one man did fall into the river in  this lego city but otherwise things were  going smoothly encouraged by these  developments dr arch was ready to begin  the true experiment introducing a  complex new variable into the  environment of the lego men and seeing  exactly how they reacted he had another  d-class build a commercial airliner out  of normal non-anomalous lego bricks and  place it just to the side of the lego  community over the following three-hour  period dr arch observed the lego man  engaging in some truly remarkable  behavior upon noticing the plane the  lego man began to form a plan they first  procured the necessary equipment from  the scp-387 tub and headed over to the  plane for a hard day's work in lego man  time at least with remarkable efficiency  the citizens of the lego community began  forming a fully functional airport  around the plain multiple runways an air  traffic control tower and even a mall  and food court within the airport itself  tiny lego attendants tried to sell  perfume to uninterested lego commuters  and lego tsa agents frisked  uncomfortable would-be lego passengers  its accuracy to the real-life airport  experience was truly brilliant but they  didn't stop there a tiny lego fuel truck  sped over to the plane and acted out the  process of refueling it a lego pilot and  his lego co-pilot climbed into the plane  and it took off literally flying around  the room without any kind of logical  propulsion system dr arch was amazed and  even then they didn't stop they  continued to build more planes of  various makes and models resulting in a  sprawling airport that if you squinted  would look just like the real thing from  this dr arch concluded that the 387 lego  man had the ability to convert  non-anomalous lego pieces into anomalous  ones he proceeded to the next experiment  for experiment 387-b dr arch decided to  switch up the d-classes and instead  brought in some of lego's more  traditional target audience a group of  10 year old children they began building  some basic constructions out of the  pieces your typical buildings people and  cars but when they realized that their  creations were actually alive their tune  immediately changed the kids spoken  hushed excited tones about a new plan  and then began putting it into practice  they built functional transformers and  just to be clear it wasn't electrical  transformers they crafted we're talking  transformers as an actual optimus prime  and megatron an m1 abrams tank and a  number of different lego weapons of mass  destruction dr arch was mortified  realizing that he'd apparently gathered  up a team of budding childhood super  villains and had them removed from the  test chamber for amnestic treatment  immediately however the second the test  chamber was vacated the kids creations  came to life and entered a state of  all-out war it was an intense battle  lasting about an hour and left no lego  survivors just a huge mess around the  room while this test was largely an  embarrassment for all involved it did  lead to some interesting new data not  only was this anomaly safe in the sense  that it didn't pose a containment breach  it was also safe in the more colloquial  sense there was no way these lego bricks  could hurt you unless you decided to eat  them and choked don't do that by the way  we see you don't scp-387 is unable to  perform dangerous actions if humans of  any age are present in the vicinity and  this arrangement goes both ways too the  lego creations will be alive and to some  extent sentient if played with  peacefully however if the human playing  with them becomes hostile then they will  immediately become inanimate so play  nice folks next came experiment 387-c  and experiment  387-c2 where dr arch turned his  attention to the tub itself since  scp-387 came into the foundation's  possession the quantity of 387 blocks  had increased how is this possible  you're probably wondering dr arch and  his team discovered an interesting  phenomena when some of the scp-387 is  placed back in the red tub but the red  tub isn't filled then 387 will  self-duplicate to fill out the tub much  like the way a gas will disperse to fill  out any containment unit it finds itself  inside however dr arch also discovered  some interesting limitations there  seemed to be no inherent anomalous  qualities to the red tub itself during  one of the experimentations dr arch  half-filled the red tub with  non-anomalous lego pieces and found that  nothing changed similarly he performed  another experiment where he placed a  single scp-387 brick into the box and  found there was no difference when he  came back dr arch and his associates  came to the conclusion that the  anomalous properties are confined solely  to the bricks themselves but they have a  kind of symbiotic relationship with the  red tub as they don't replicate in any  other containment units in order to  activate replication the 387 must cover  the entire bottom layer of the tub next  came experiment  387-d where dr arch hoped to test the  specific activation mechanisms of  scp-387  the lego creations animated whenever  they were assembled by a child or an  adult so it wasn't an age-regulated  anomaly the next experiment involved  using a remotely controlled robotic arm  to create a lego construction to see if  the mere act of construction itself was  enough to instigate 387's primary  anomalous effect however this didn't  turn out to be the case the robotic arm  assembled lego construction never came  alive dr arch's next hypothesis was that  perhaps flesh was needed to activate  scp-387 but how could he test using  flesh without just having a normal human  assemble the lego pieces thankfully the  answer came to dr arch by total accident  a few cells over an anomaly trying to  breach containment had just killed a  foundation agent trying to stand in its  way while the d-classes cleaned up the  mess dr arch dragged the body over to  where the 387 tests were being conducted  and meticulously puppeteered its arms  and hands to put together more 387 lego  constructions but once again it didn't  come to life interesting next hypothesis  maybe it needs warmth to activate in a  move that proved unpopular with  co-workers just trying to eat their  pre-packaged sandwiches in the site 19  break room dr arch dragged the dead  foundation agent's body over towards the  room's radiator and leaned its arms and  hands over the top of it for 20 minutes  before giving his newly discovered  puppeteering skills another go but once  again nothing happened dr arch concluded  that perhaps human psychic energy or  maybe an active pulse was what caused  387 to activate if you're waiting for  the horrifying twist well aside from the  puppeteering of a dead coworker's limbs  we're pleased to tell you that there  just isn't one this time  scp-387 serves no containment breach  risk and no risk of harm to foundation  personnel in fact playing with the  living lego has led to an 87 percent  increase in morale for foundation staff  so as long as you fill in the proper  forms and tidy up afterwards you're  actually allowed to play with the  scp-387 anytime you want after all  working for the scp foundation is a  stressful job and really we're all  children at heart oh and there was one  more experiment experiment 387-e where  lego community was built using scp-387  and then a pile of mega bloks lego's  most common imitator was introduced into  the mix the lego men of the community  really weren't pleased by this while the  actual details of what happened have  thankfully been expunged the one clue to  what may have happened came from a note  left by dr arch that's right the  puppeteer guy his notes on that  experiment were four simple words oh no  not again now go check out  scp-1007 mr life and mr death and  scp-5094 miss j's wizkid schoolhouse for  more fascinating safe class scps

